    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The order of operations (PEMDAS/BODMAS) tells us to solve the multiplication and division before the addition and subtraction. So we have $1+6\\cdot2-3+5\\cdot4\\div2$. Multiplying we get $12-3+10\\div2$ $12-3+5$ then subtraction 9+5 which equals to 14. So the final answer is $\\boxed{14}$.\n#\nTo solve the expression \\(1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2\\), we need to follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Multiplication and Division**: Perform these operations from left to right.\n   \\[\n   6 \\cdot 2 = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5 \\cdot 4 = 20\n   \\]\n   So the expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   1 + 12 - 3 + 20 \\div 2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Division**: Next, perform the division.\n   \\[\n   20 \\div 2 = 10\n   \\]\n   So the expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   1 + 12 - 3 + 10\n   \\]\n\n3. **Addition and Subtraction**: Perform these operations from left to right.\n   \\[\n   1 + 12 = 13\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   13 - 3 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   10 + 10 = 20\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
