    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We need to solve the given arithmetic expression step by step, adhering to the order of operations (PEMDAS), which stands for Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right).\n\nStep 1: Perform multiplication and division from left to right.\n\\[\n5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2 = 20 \\div 2 = 10.\n\\]\nThe expression now is:\n\\[\n1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 10.\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Perform multiplication after the first division.\n\\[\n6 \\cdot 2 = 12.\n\\]\nThe expression now is:\n\\[\n1 + 12 - 3 + 10.\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Perform addition and subtraction from left to right.\n\\[\n1 + 12 = 13,\n\\]\n\\[\n13 - 3 = 10,\n\\]\n\\[\n10 + 10 = 20.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression $1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{20}.\n\\]",
